    "explanation": "To both parties: the route deviation on this trip is established on the evidence, and the fare is recomputed arithmetically. To the rider: you are refunded SGD 13.70 of the SGD 21.48 charged, not the whole amount. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02824) is not impaired for policy purposes — 131 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gap above 90 seconds, no jump above 500 m — and it measures 14.4 km between the recorded pickup and drop-off against the platform's booked optimal of 2.4 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02824). That is an excess of 12.0 km, 500% of optimal and twelve times the 0.8 km absolute floor, so both limbs of POL-RD-01 pass and the deviation is material; POL-RD-06's driver-profile check was run and shows 0 deviation flags over 210 completed trips in the trailing 90 days, so no repeat-pattern uplift and no conduct referral arise. Read off the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02824): charged_total is SGD 21.48; recomputed_fare is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 2.4 + 0.28 x 5.0) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + SGD 0.80 platform fee = SGD 7.80; the refund is 21.48 - 7.80 = SGD 13.68, rounded up to SGD 13.70. That is 63.7% of what you paid, below the 90% share that would substitute a full refund, and well above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 13.70 and the full SGD 21.48 you asked for is not attainable on any line of this fare. There is no ERP or toll charge on the ledger (on-route and off-route ERP totals are both SGD 0.00 and no gantry was crossed), so nothing is added on that account; POL-RD-09(1) would in any case forbid stacking such a line on the POL-RD-02 figure. This is a metered fare and not a pooled trip, so POL-RD-11 and POL-RD-12 do not apply. To the driver: your account that the rider changed the destination verbally does not carry the trip. POL-RD-04 requires a rider instruction recorded in this trip's chat log; the chat log (EV-CHAT-02824) contains zero messages, so there is no instruction, no timestamp to test under POL-RD-04(b) and no chat_message.waypoint_hint to run the 200 m corroboration test against — the clause is unavailable on this record and the excess is measured against the booked 2.4 km optimal route. POL-RD-05 requires an amended endpoint and the stored amended optimal; pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km are all null, so the amendment cannot be run and no substitute figure may be derived. No advisory covered this trip (EV-ADVIS-02824-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), no party asserted a traffic cause, and POL-RD-03 therefore exonerates nothing. The finding rests on artifacts all at weight 1.0 — the GPS trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown — so confidence is 0.95. The monetary effect of SGD 13.70 is above the SGD 8.00 automatic execution threshold; under POL-GEN-05 the ruling issues but the amount is held and the case is queued for human release."
